{"_v":3,"id":"inside-no-9-stage-fright-west-end-2025","cat":"west-end","bd":{"positive":1,"mixed":3,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Annabel Nugent","o":"The Independent","s":82,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/theatre-dance/reviews/inside-no-9-stage-fright-review-b2689116.html","q":"Expect everything you love from the shows here: accents, slapstick, wigs, false teeth. It’s old-school laughs that still do the trick. As one of the younger members of the crowd, I suspect a good few references went over my head."},{"cn":"Sam Marlowe","o":"The Stage","s":57,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/reviews/inside-no-9-stagefright-review-wyndhams-theatre-london-reece-shearsmith-steve-pemberton-simon-evans","q":"Fans will enjoy unpicking its snarl of tangled entrails"},{"cn":"Helen Hawkins","o":"The Arts Desk","s":72,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://theartsdesk.com/theatre/inside-no-9-stage-fright-wyndham%E2%80%99s-review-uneven-fright-night-f%C3%AAted-duo","q":"Still inventive and fun but short on sharp shocks"},{"cn":"Anya Ryan","o":"London Theatre","s":57,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.londontheatre.co.uk/reviews/inside-no-9-stage-fright-review-wyndhams-theatre","q":"Diehard fans are sure to be satisfied"}],"pd":"2025-01-18"}